# T-Office Project Product Requirements Document (PRD)

## 1. Overview

T-Office is a comprehensive internal office management platform designed to streamline administrative, human resources, inventory, and collaboration workflows within organizations. This full-stack solution centralizes key operational functions into a single unified system with robust role-based access control, providing a seamless experience for employees across all departments.

The platform offers a modern web interface with Progressive Web App (PWA) support, enabling offline functionality and mobile accessibility. Built with cutting-edge technologies including Next.js for the frontend and Express.js for the backend, T-Office delivers enterprise-grade performance with intuitive user experience.

## 2. Problem Statement

Organizations today face significant challenges with fragmented internal tools and inefficient workflows:

- **Tool Fragmentation**: Multiple disconnected systems for HR, inventory, communications, and administration lead to productivity losses and data silos
- **Inflexible Permissions**: Traditional access control systems fail to provide granular, department-specific permissions
- **Manual Processes**: Paper-based or spreadsheet-driven workflows for onboarding, inventory tracking, and approvals are error-prone and time-consuming
- **Limited Accessibility**: Lack of offline support restricts productivity for remote workers or those in low-connectivity environments
- **Inconsistent User Experience**: Disparate tools with varying interfaces increase training overhead and reduce adoption rates

These challenges result in decreased productivity, increased operational costs, and reduced employee satisfaction.

## 3. Goals

### Primary Goals
1. **Centralize Operations**: Unify HR, inventory, communication, and administrative functions in a single platform
2. **Enhance Security**: Implement fine-grained role-based access control with department-level permissions
3. **Improve Productivity**: Streamline workflows with automated processes and intuitive interfaces
4. **Enable Mobility**: Provide offline functionality and responsive design for remote work capability
5. **Reduce Operational Costs**: Eliminate the need for multiple specialized tools and reduce manual processes

### Success Metrics
- 40% reduction in time spent on administrative tasks
- 95% system uptime
- <500ms average page load time
- 90% user adoption rate within 3 months of deployment
- Zero security incidents related to unauthorized access

## 4. Personas

### 4.1 HR Manager (Sarah)
- **Role**: Human Resources Director
- **Responsibilities**: Employee onboarding, performance management, policy enforcement
- **Needs**: Comprehensive employee data access, automated onboarding workflows, HR analytics
- **Technical Proficiency**: Intermediate
- **Key Goals**: Ensure compliance, streamline hiring processes, maintain employee records

### 4.2 Inventory Coordinator (Michael)
- **Role**: Warehouse/Inventory Manager
- **Responsibilities**: Product tracking, stock management, supplier coordination
- **Needs**: Real-time inventory visibility, automated alerts, reporting capabilities
- **Technical Proficiency**: Basic
- **Key Goals**: Prevent stockouts, optimize warehouse space, track product lifecycles

### 4.3 Department Head (Jennifer)
- **Role**: Department Manager
- **Responsibilities**: Team management, resource allocation, performance monitoring
- **Needs**: Department-specific dashboards, team analytics, communication tools
- **Technical Proficiency**: Basic
- **Key Goals**: Improve team productivity, allocate resources effectively, monitor KPIs

### 4.4 General Employee (David)
- **Role**: Standard Employee
- **Responsibilities**: Daily tasks, time tracking, accessing company resources
- **Needs**: Simple interface, quick access to relevant information, self-service capabilities
- **Technical Proficiency**: Basic
- **Key Goals**: Complete tasks efficiently, access required resources, communicate with team

### 4.5 System Administrator (Robert)
- **Role**: IT/System Administrator
- **Responsibilities**: Platform maintenance, user management, security oversight
- **Needs**: Comprehensive system controls, monitoring tools, audit capabilities
- **Technical Proficiency**: Advanced
- **Key Goals**: Maintain system reliability, ensure data security, manage user access

## 5. User Stories

### 5.1 Authentication & Access Control
As a user, I want to securely log in to the system so that I can access my authorized features.
As an administrator, I want to control user access at both department and role levels so that I can ensure appropriate permissions.
As an employee, I want to see only the features relevant to my role so that I'm not overwhelmed by unnecessary options.

### 5.2 Dashboard & Navigation
As a user, I want a personalized dashboard showing my relevant tasks and notifications so that I can quickly understand my priorities.
As a department head, I want to see team performance metrics on my dashboard so that I can monitor department health.
As a new user, I want an intuitive navigation system so that I can easily find the features I need.

### 5.3 HR Management
As an HR manager, I want to onboard new employees through a guided workflow so that all required information is collected consistently.
As an HR manager, I want to offboard departing employees through a systematic process so that all access and assets are properly managed.
As an employee, I want to submit HR queries through the system so that I can get timely responses.
As a manager, I want to view my team members' details so that I can manage them effectively.
As a user, I want to receive notifications for HR-related actions so that I'm informed of important updates.

### 5.4 Inventory Management
As an inventory coordinator, I want to track products from procurement to distribution so that I can maintain optimal stock levels.
As a department head, I want to view inventory reports so that I can make informed purchasing decisions.
As a user, I want to request items from inventory so that I can get the resources I need for my work.

### 5.5 Communication
As a team member, I want to communicate with colleagues through an integrated chat system so that I can collaborate effectively.
As a moderator, I want to manage chat conversations so that I can maintain a professional environment.
As a user, I want to receive important announcements so that I stay informed about company updates.

### 5.6 Knowledge Management
As an employee, I want to access department-specific documentation so that I can find the information I need.
As a subject matter expert, I want to contribute to the company wiki so that I can share my knowledge.
As a new hire, I want to complete mandatory training modules so that I can get up to speed quickly.

### 5.7 Time Tracking
As an employee, I want to clock in and out through the system so that my attendance is recorded accurately.
As a manager, I want to view team attendance reports so that I can monitor punctuality.
As an administrator, I want to manage clock-in locations so that I can control where employees can clock in.

## 6. Functional Requirements

### 6.1 Authentication & Session Management
1. Secure user registration with email verification
2. JWT-based authentication with 1-hour token expiration
3. Automatic token refresh 5 minutes before expiration
4. Password reset functionality with email verification
5. Single sign-on (SSO) readiness for enterprise integration

### 6.2 Dashboard & Navigation
1. Personalized dashboard with role-based widgets
2. Collapsible navigation sidebar with department-specific sections
3. Real-time notifications and alerts
4. Quick access toolbar for frequently used functions
5. Theme customization (light/dark mode)

### 6.3 HR Management
1. Employee onboarding workflow with multi-step forms
2. Employee offboarding workflow with asset tracking and access revocation
3. Digital personnel file management
4. HR query submission and tracking system
5. Performance review management
6. Training and certification tracking
7. Attendance and leave management
8. Automated notifications for HR processes (approvals, completions, deadlines)

### 6.4 Inventory Management
1. Complete product lifecycle tracking (inbound → storage → outbound)
2. Serial number tracking for individual items
3. Supplier and vendor management
4. Automated low-stock alerts
5. Barcode scanning integration capability
6. Comprehensive reporting and analytics
7. Notification system for inventory thresholds and status changes

### 6.5 Communication
1. Real-time team chat with file sharing
2. Private messaging between users
3. Channel-based conversations for departments/projects
4. Message moderation tools for administrators
5. Chat history retention and search
6. Notification system for mentions and direct messages
7. Announcement broadcasting with read receipts

### 6.6 Knowledge Management
1. Department-specific wiki with hierarchical organization
2. Rich text editing with media embedding
3. Version control for documentation
4. Search functionality across all knowledge base content
5. Progress tracking for mandatory training
6. Access controls for sensitive documentation
7. Notification system for wiki updates and mentions

### 6.7 Time Tracking
1. Geofenced clock-in/clock-out functionality
2. Location management for clock-in points
3. Attendance reporting with export capabilities
4. Overtime calculation and tracking
5. Integration with payroll systems (future)
6. Mobile-friendly time entry
7. Notification system for clock-in reminders and anomalies

### 6.8 Administration
1. Department management with hierarchical organization
2. Role-based access control with granular permissions
3. User management with bulk operations
4. System configuration and customization
5. Audit logging for all system activities
6. Data backup and recovery procedures
7. Notification system for system alerts and maintenance

### 6.9 Notification System
1. Centralized notification center with filtering and sorting
2. Real-time notifications with visual indicators
3. Email notifications for critical events
4. Configurable notification preferences per user
5. Notification history and archiving
6. Priority levels for different notification types
7. Integration with all system modules

## 7. Non-Functional Requirements

### 7.1 Performance
1. Page load times under 500ms for 95% of requests
2. Support for 1,000 concurrent users
3. Database query response times under 100ms for standard operations
4. Real-time chat updates with <200ms latency
5. Offline functionality for critical operations

### 7.2 Security
1. End-to-end encryption for data in transit
2. Role-based access control enforced at both UI and API layers
3. Regular security audits and penetration testing
4. Compliance with GDPR and other relevant data protection regulations
5. Two-factor authentication support

### 7.3 Reliability
1. 99.9% system uptime
2. Automated failover for critical services
3. Comprehensive error handling and recovery mechanisms
4. Regular automated backups with point-in-time recovery
5. Monitoring and alerting for system health

### 7.4 Scalability
1. Horizontal scaling support for frontend components
2. Database connection pooling for backend services
3. CDN integration for static assets
4. Microservices-ready architecture
5. Containerized deployment with Docker support

### 7.5 Usability
1. WCAG 2.1 AA compliance for accessibility
2. Responsive design supporting desktop, tablet, and mobile devices
3. Intuitive user interface with minimal learning curve
4. Comprehensive help system and documentation
5. Multi-language support (future enhancement)

## 8. System Architecture Summary

T-Office follows a hybrid full-stack monolith architecture with clear separation between frontend and backend components:

### 8.1 Frontend Architecture
- **Framework**: Next.js 13.5.1 with App Router for server-side rendering
- **Language**: TypeScript with React 18.2.0
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS with component-based design system
- **State Management**: React Context API with custom hooks
- **UI Components**: Radix UI primitives for accessible components

### 8.2 Backend Architecture
- **Runtime**: Node.js 18 with Express.js framework
- **Database**: PostgreSQL with connection pooling
- **Authentication**: JWT-based token system
- **API Design**: RESTful endpoints with consistent resource naming
- **Middleware**: Custom authentication and validation layers

### 8.3 Infrastructure
- **Deployment**: Docker containerization with docker-compose orchestration
- **Development**: Concurrent development servers for frontend and backend
- **Environment Management**: Environment-specific configuration files
- **Monitoring**: Integrated logging and error tracking

## 9. Constraints

### 9.1 Technical Constraints
1. Must support Node.js v18+ environments
2. Database limited to PostgreSQL compatibility
3. Browser support restricted to modern browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge)
4. Mobile support limited to iOS 12+ and Android 8+
5. File upload size limited to 10MB per file

### 9.2 Business Constraints
1. Must comply with company data privacy policies
2. Integration with existing HRIS systems required (Phase 2)
3. Budget limitations restrict third-party service dependencies
4. Deployment must support on-premises hosting
5. Training materials must be available in English initially

### 9.3 Resource Constraints
1. Development team limited to 5 full-time engineers
2. QA resources limited to 2 dedicated testers
3. Project timeline constrained to 6 months for initial release
4. Hosting infrastructure budget limited to $500/month
5. Third-party API usage restricted to free-tier services

## 10. Assumptions

### 10.1 Technical Assumptions
1. Organization has stable internet connectivity for cloud services
2. Users have modern browsers with JavaScript enabled
3. IT department can support Docker-based deployments
4. PostgreSQL database meets performance requirements
5. SSL certificates will be provided for production deployment

### 10.2 User Assumptions
1. Users have basic computer literacy skills
2. Department heads will adopt the system as workflow improvement tool
3. Employees will engage with training materials voluntarily
4. Administrators will regularly maintain system configurations
5. Feedback mechanisms will be utilized for continuous improvement

### 10.3 Business Assumptions
1. Executive leadership supports digital transformation initiative
2. Budget allocation will continue throughout development lifecycle
3. Change management program will facilitate user adoption
4. Legal department approves data handling procedures
5. Integration requirements will remain stable during development

## 11. Acceptance Criteria

### 11.1 Core Functionality
1. User can successfully register, login, and access authorized features
2. All role-based access controls function as configured by administrators
3. Dashboard loads within 500ms for 95% of users
4. HR onboarding and offboarding workflows complete without errors
5. Inventory transactions are tracked accurately from inbound to outbound

### 11.2 Performance Benchmarks
1. System supports 100 concurrent users with <200ms response times
2. Database backup completes within 10 minutes for datasets <1GB
3. Offline functionality works for minimum 24 hours without connectivity
4. Mobile interface loads within 1 second on 3G networks
5. File uploads complete within 30 seconds for 5MB files

### 11.3 Security Requirements
1. Unauthorized access attempts are logged and blocked
2. Passwords are properly hashed and salted in database
3. JWT tokens expire as configured and cannot be reused
4. Data transmission is encrypted in transit
5. User sessions terminate after 8 hours of inactivity

### 11.4 Usability Standards
1. New users can complete basic tasks after 30 minutes of training
2. Accessibility audit scores 90%+ on automated testing tools
3. Mobile interface functions equivalently to desktop version
4. Error messages provide actionable guidance to users
5. Help documentation covers all major functionality

## 12. Release Milestones

### Phase 1: Foundation (Months 1-2)
- Core authentication and authorization system
- Basic dashboard with navigation
- Department and role management
- Initial user management features
- Database schema and migration system
- **Success Criteria**: MVP with secure login and basic access control

### Phase 2: HR & Administration (Months 2-3)
- Complete HR management module
- Employee onboarding and offboarding workflows
- HR query system
- Administrative controls and reporting
- User profile management
- Basic notification system
- **Success Criteria**: Fully functional HR department workflow

### Phase 3: Inventory Management (Months 3-4)
- Complete inventory tracking system
- Product lifecycle management
- Reporting and analytics
- Import/export functionality
- Barcode scanning preparation
- Enhanced notification integration
- **Success Criteria**: End-to-end inventory management capability

### Phase 4: Communication & Collaboration (Months 4-5)
- Internal chat system with channels
- Wiki and knowledge base
- Notification system
- File sharing capabilities
- **Success Criteria**: Integrated communication platform

### Phase 5: Time Tracking & Polish (Month 6)
- Time and attendance tracking
- Geofencing functionality
- Mobile optimization
- Performance optimization
- User acceptance testing
- **Success Criteria**: Production-ready system meeting all requirements

### Phase 6: Deployment & Training (Month 6)
- Production deployment
- User training program
- Documentation completion
- Go-live support
- **Success Criteria**: Successful system adoption with >80% user engagement

